-- title:
--   Existence of a Mumford tower for a type-preserving Schottky group
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ be irreducible, and assume the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements; let $K_0$ be a field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ be the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$ (image of $\pi$ under $\mathcal{O} \to K_0$), and let $N \le \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be a subgroup which acts on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathcal{O} \subset K_0$ — the graph on homothety classes of full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices in $K_0^2$ with adjacency generated by the relation `AdjacentLattice` — in Schottky fashion, i.e. every vertex stabiliser in $N$ is trivial, no element of $N$ carries a dart to its reverse, and $N$ has finitely many orbits of vertices and of darts; assume moreover that every element of $N$ preserves the parity of the graph distance to the vertex of the standard lattice. Then the type `MumfordTower` $\mathcal{O}\,\pi\,K_0\,r\,g_1\,N$ is nonempty: there exist schemes $Z_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal{O}/(\pi^{n+1})$ whose structure morphisms are proper and flat, with transition morphisms $Z_n \to Z_{n+1}$ forming pullback squares over the quotient maps of the base, such that every finite subset of $Z_n$ lies in an affine open, together with maps $q_n$ sending a Deligne datum (a point of the formal upper half-plane functor $\Omega$) over an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $B$ to a $B$-point of $Z_n$, compatible with the base, functorial in $B$, compatible with the transitions, invariant under the $N$-action on Deligne data, and with the further chart conditions (open immersions from the localised chart rings `chartERing`, and the remaining fields of the structure) summarised here.
--
--   This is the existence of Mumford's formal model of the quotient $N \backslash \hat{\Omega}$ as a tower of proper flat schemes over $\mathcal{O}/(\pi^{n+1})$, for a type-preserving Schottky group $N$ acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree of a discrete valuation ring with residue field of prime order. It feeds the construction of formal quotient data in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, being used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib).
